
@rule board.first.lunch.gentle
on board
when kind=lunch tone=gentle
- I, um... forgot my lunch today. And I don't really like eating alone...
- I left my bento at home... and eating by myself feels so lonely.
- Um, I forgot my lunch... would anyone share a table with me?
- No lunch today... and no one to sit with. Ehe...

@rule board.first.lunch.energetic
on board
when kind=lunch tone=energetic
- I forgot my bento! And nobody to eat with! Tragic!
- No bento AND no lunch buddy?! Worst day!
- My lunch is at home and I'm starving! Someone save me!
- Forgot my food! Who's eating with me?!

@rule board.first.lunch.cool
on board
when kind=lunch tone=cool
- I forgot my lunch. Eating alone is fine. ...Mostly.
- No lunch today. Company would be... acceptable.
- I forgot my bento. I wouldn't mind a lunch partner.
- Lunch alone again. I'd tolerate company.

@rule board.first.lunch.teasing
on board
when kind=lunch tone=teasing
- Lunch alone again today. How sad for me~
- Forgot my lunch. Someone could feed me~
- Lunch for one again. Pity me~
- No bento, no buddy. Someone fix that.

@rule board.first.study.gentle
on board
when kind=study tone=gentle
- I don't understand today's lesson at all... I'm scared about the test.
- Today's lesson went right over my head... the test scares me.
- I'm so behind... would someone study with me?
- I don't get any of it... I'm worried about the exam.

@rule board.first.study.energetic
on board
when kind=study tone=energetic
- I'm SO lost in class! Help me study?!
- Class today?! Total mystery! Study buddy wanted!
- I'm drowning in assignments! Throw me a rope!
- Test incoming and I know NOTHING! Help!

@rule board.first.study.cool
on board
when kind=study tone=cool
- I'm behind in class. I'd study better with someone.
- I fell behind. A study partner would help.
- I need to review. Preferably not alone.
- The material is dense. I'd study better with someone.

@rule board.first.study.teasing
on board
when kind=study tone=teasing
- The test is going to destroy me. Unless someone helps.
- The exam will crush me. Unless a hero appears~
- I need a tutor. A cute one.
- If I fail, it's everyone's fault. Help me~

@rule board.first.exercise.gentle
on board
when kind=exercise tone=gentle
- I want to get a little stronger... but working out alone is hard.
- I want to get stronger... but exercising alone is hard.
- I'd like to train a little... if someone came with me.
- Working out by myself is lonely... and hard.

@rule board.first.exercise.energetic
on board
when kind=exercise tone=energetic
- I've got too much energy! I need to move!
- I'm bursting with energy! Someone run with me!
- I need to MOVE! Training partner, anyone?!
- Let's work out! Somebody! Anybody!

@rule board.first.exercise.cool
on board
when kind=exercise tone=cool
- I want to train, but alone it's boring.
- I want to train. Alone, it's tedious.
- I need a sparring partner.
- Training is better with a rival.

@rule board.first.exercise.teasing
on board
when kind=exercise tone=teasing
- I need a training partner. One who can keep up.
- I need someone to train with. Someone who won't cry.
- Training partner wanted. Must keep up.
- Who's brave enough to train with me?

@rule board.first.club.gentle
on board
when kind=club tone=gentle
- I'd like to do something with the club... if that's okay.
- I'd love to do something for the club... if someone helps.
- Could we do a little club activity? I'd be happy.
- I have a small idea for the club... if that's okay.

@rule board.first.club.energetic
on board
when kind=club tone=energetic
- Let's do club stuff! I'm bored of waiting!
- Club time! I'm tired of waiting around!
- Let's do club stuff! Right now!
- The club needs action! Let's go!

@rule board.first.club.cool
on board
when kind=club tone=cool
- I have an idea for the club. I need a hand.
- I have a plan for the club. I need help.
- A club task needs doing. Volunteers?
- The club needs attention. I'll need a hand.

@rule board.first.club.teasing
on board
when kind=club tone=teasing
- The club's been quiet. Let's change that.
- The club's gotten boring. Let's spice it up.
- Let's shake the club up a bit.
- Club's too quiet. I have ideas~

@rule board.first.walkhome.gentle
on board
when kind=walkhome tone=gentle
- The way home gets dark early... I don't like walking it alone.
- It gets dark so early... I don't want to walk home alone.
- The road home is scary at night...
- Walking home alone makes me nervous...

@rule board.first.walkhome.energetic
on board
when kind=walkhome tone=energetic
- Walking home alone is so boring!
- Walking home solo is SO boring! Company?!
- Someone walk with me! I'll talk the whole way!
- Who's going my way? Let's walk!

@rule board.first.walkhome.cool
on board
when kind=walkhome tone=cool
- I'd rather not walk home alone today.
- I'd prefer company on the way home.
- Walking home alone isn't ideal today.
- Company for the walk home would be welcome.

@rule board.first.walkhome.teasing
on board
when kind=walkhome tone=teasing
- If someone walked me home, I wouldn't complain.
- A gentleman would walk me home. Hint.
- Someone could escort me home. Just saying~
- Walking me home earns points. Big ones.

@rule board.first.gift.gentle
on board
when kind=gift tone=gentle
- It's been a hard day... I wish something nice would happen.
- Today was hard... I wish something nice would happen.
- I'm a little down... something sweet would help.
- It's been one of those days...

@rule board.first.gift.energetic
on board
when kind=gift tone=energetic
- Ugh, today needs a treat! Like, badly!
- Today was rough! I need a treat! Now!
- Ugh, I need a pick-me-up! Big time!
- Bad day! Cheer me up, somebody!

@rule board.first.gift.cool
on board
when kind=gift tone=cool
- I could use something to lift my mood.
- Today was trying. Something pleasant would help.
- I could use a distraction.
- A small kindness would be welcome today.

@rule board.first.gift.teasing
on board
when kind=gift tone=teasing
- A little present would fix my mood. Just saying.
- A gift would fix everything. Just saying.
- My mood needs fixing. Presents work.
- Cheer me up and I'll owe you~

@rule board.first.meetat.gentle
on board
when kind=meetat tone=gentle
- Would you meet me at the {place} sometime today?
- Could you come to the {place} later?
- I'll be at the {place}... would you come?
- Um, meet me at the {place} today?

@rule board.first.meetat.energetic
on board
when kind=meetat tone=energetic
- Meet me at the {place} later, okay?!
- The {place}! Later! Be there!
- See you at the {place}, okay?!
- Come to the {place} later! Promise!

@rule board.first.meetat.cool
on board
when kind=meetat tone=cool
- Come by the {place} later.
- The {place}. Later today.
- I'll be at the {place}. Come.
- Meet me at the {place}.

@rule board.first.meetat.teasing
on board
when kind=meetat tone=teasing
- The {place}. Later. Don't be late.
- {place}. Later. I'll be waiting~
- Find me at the {place}. If you dare.
- The {place}. Don't keep me waiting.

@rule board.first.errand.gentle
on board
when kind=errand tone=gentle
- Could I ask a small favor? {@errand}
- Um, a small favor, please? {@errand}
- Would you help me with something? {@errand}
- If it's not too much... {@errand}

@rule board.first.errand.energetic
on board
when kind=errand tone=energetic
- Favor time! {@errand}
- Help help! {@errand}
- I need you! {@errand}
- Quick favor! {@errand}

@rule board.first.errand.cool
on board
when kind=errand tone=cool
- I need a favor. {@errand}
- A request. {@errand}
- Help me with this. {@errand}
- Something I need. {@errand}

@rule board.first.errand.teasing
on board
when kind=errand tone=teasing
- You owe me, remember? {@errand}
- Do me a favor~ {@errand}
- I'm calling in a favor. {@errand}
- You'll do this for me, right? {@errand}

# Her errand in her own words, for {@errand} above: errandat is where it is, reqsrc who posted it.
@rule errand.library
on @errand
when errandat=library reqsrc=board
- [My library books are overdue. Could you return them for me?|Could you take my books back to the library? They're late.|My library books... they were due last week.]
- [The librarian keeps asking for my books. Could you take them back?|Return my books to the library? I'll pay the late fee myself.|If my library books are late again, I'm banned. Help?]

@rule errand.cafeteria
on @errand
when errandat=cafeteria reqsrc=board
- [Could you get me a melon bread before they sell out?|The cafeteria melon bread. I need one. Before it's gone.|Grab me a melon bread? They always run out.]
- [One melon bread from the cafeteria. Just one. Please?|If you're near the cafeteria, a melon bread would save my day.|They only bake a few melon breads. Could you get one for me?]
- [Melon bread. Cafeteria. Before the rush. Please.|If the cafeteria still has melon bread, get me one?] [I'll pay you back.|You're a lifesaver.]

@rule errand.staffroom
on @errand
when errandat=staffroom reqsrc=board
- [Could you turn in my assignments at the faculty room?|My assignments need to go to the faculty room.|Take my assignments to the faculty room? I can't face them today.]
- [My assignments are done, but I can't make myself walk into the faculty room.|Could you drop my assignments on the teacher's desk in the faculty room?|The faculty room wants my assignments today. Could you take them?]

@rule errand.clubroom
on @errand
when errandat=clubroom reqsrc=board
- [I left my notebook in the club room. Could you get it?|My notebook's still in the club room...|Fetch my notebook from the club room?]
- [My notebook's on the club room table, I think. Could you bring it?|I need my notebook from the club room before class.|Could you check the club room? My notebook has all my notes.]

@rule errand.gym
on @errand
when errandat=gym reqsrc=board
- [I left my towel in the gym. Could you find it?|My towel's somewhere in the gym.|Find my towel in the gym? I forgot it after practice.]
- [My towel's probably on the gym bench. Could you look?|I left my towel in the gym again. Could you get it?|Could you find my towel in the gym before someone throws it out?]

@rule errand.pool
on @errand
when errandat=pool reqsrc=board
- [My goggles are still at the pool. Could you get them?|I forgot my goggles at the pool...|Get my goggles back from the pool?]
- [My goggles should be by the pool's edge. Could you get them?|Could you check the pool for my goggles? Blue ones.|I can't swim without my goggles. They're at the pool.]

@rule errand.infirmary
on @errand
when errandat=infirmary reqsrc=board
- [Could you pick up my medicine at the infirmary?|My medicine's waiting at the infirmary.|The infirmary has my medicine. Could you get it for me?]
- [The nurse has my medicine ready. Could you pick it up?|Could you get my medicine from the infirmary? I'm not feeling great.|My medicine's at the infirmary, and I can't leave class.]

@rule errand.classroom
on @errand
when errandat=classroom reqsrc=board
- [Could you copy today's notes for me?|I missed today's notes. Could you copy them?|Today's notes... I didn't get any of them down.]
- [Could you copy the notes from today's class for me?|I zoned out all class. Could you copy the notes for me?|Lend me today's notes? Or copy them? Please?]

@rule errand.charm
on @errand
when reqsrc=arc
- [I lost my charm. Someone saw one at the {place}.|My charm's gone. Someone said it's at the {place}.|My little charm... it might be at the {place}.]
- [My good-luck charm fell off my bag. Someone saw it at the {place}.|I had a charm on my bag... someone found one at the {place}.|My charm! It might be at the {place}. Please?]
- [My good-luck charm is missing. Maybe at the {place}?|I think I left my charm at the {place}.] [Could you look?|I feel naked without it.]

@rule errand.any
on @errand
- [Could you go to the {place} for me?|There's something at the {place} I need.|I need something done at the {place}.]
- [Could you run over to the {place}? I'd owe you.|There's something at the {place} I need. Could you go?|Do you have time to go to the {place} for me?]
- [Would you stop by the {place} for me?|Could you check the {place}? I can't get away.] [I'll owe you one.|It won't take long.]

@rule board.first.other.gentle
on board
when tone=gentle
- Could we talk again later today? There's something I want to tell you.
- Could we talk later? I have something to tell you.
- Please find me later today... I want to tell you something.
- Later, could we talk a little? It's important to me.

@rule board.first.other.energetic
on board
when tone=energetic
- Come find me later! I've got stuff to tell you!
- Find me later! Big news!
- Later! Come find me! I have stuff!
- Don't forget to find me later!

@rule board.first.other.cool
on board
when tone=cool
- Talk to me again later. It's important.
- Later. We need to talk.
- Find me later today.
- We'll talk later. It matters.

@rule board.first.other.teasing
on board
when tone=teasing
- Find me later. I have something to say.
- Later. Come find me. Alone.
- I have something to say. Later.
- Find me later. Don't make me wait.
